  "key_facts": [
    "Michael actively participates in diversity activities, introduces humor, and criticizes the seminars.",
    "Takes an active role in choosing the health care plan and plans a staff trip.",
    "Expresses his enjoyment of playing basketball as a way to forget work stress and emphasizes lessons about character and life.",
    "Shows interest in Katy and considers giving her a ride home, with some uncertainty about his feelings.",
    "Hosts the Dundies, gives awards, and makes jokes.",
    "Expresses frustration about restrictions on his speech and humor, and declares he can no longer be friends with colleagues.",
    "Decides to sign the mortgage and feels satisfied with his decision to become a homeowner.",
    "Discusses Ryan's evaluation and explains the 'women and children first' rule during the fire drill.",
    "Expresses the heavy burden of firing someone and improvises in stressful situations.",
    "Michael challenges Jim to a fight and discusses his emergency contact.",
    "Admits to making out with Jan and discusses their interaction.",
    "Engages in a complicated interaction with Jan involving kissing and business, questions his appearance's impact on Jan's feelings."
